      "text": "97,662.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **131** and **742**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 131 by 2 (the ones place digit of 742):**\n   \n   \\[\n   131 \\times 2 = 262\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 131 by 40 (the tens place digit of 742):**\n   \n   \\[\n   131 \\times 40 = 5240\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 131 by 700 (the hundreds place digit of 742):**\n   \n   \\[\n   131 \\times 700 = 91700\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   262 + 5240 + 91700 = 97,662\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{97,\\!662}\n\\]",
