      "index": 0,
      "text": "340,070.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **370** and **917**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 370 by each digit of 917\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   370 \\times 7 = 2590\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (1), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   370 \\times 10 = 3700\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (9), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   370 \\times 900 = 333000\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n2590 + 3700 + 333000 = 340070\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{340070}\n\\]",
