      "text": "72,320.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **280** and **259**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 280 by 9 (the ones place digit of 259):**\n   \n   \\[\n   280 \\times 9 = 2520\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 280 by 50 (the tens place digit of 259):**\n   \n   \\[\n   280 \\times 50 = 14,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 280 by 200 (the hundreds place digit of 259):**\n   \n   \\[\n   280 \\times 200 = 56,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2,\\!520 + 14,\\!000 + 56,\\!000 = 72,\\!520\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{72,\\!520}\n\\]",
