      "text": "194,308.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **622** and **314**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 622 by 4 (the ones place digit of 314)\n\\[\n622 \\times 4 = 2488\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 622 by 10 (the tens place digit of 314)\n\\[\n622 \\times 10 = 6220\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 622 by 300 (the hundreds place digit of 314)\n\\[\n622 \\times 300 = 186600\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum all the results\n\\[\n2488 + 6220 + 186600 = 194308\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{194308}\n\\]",
