      "text": "631,150.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **971** and **650**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 971 by 0 (the ones place digit of 650):**\n   \n   \\[\n   971 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 971 by 50 (the tens place digit of 650):**\n   \n   \\[\n   971 \\times 50 = 48,\\!550\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 971 by 600 (the hundreds place digit of 650):**\n   \n   \\[\n   971 \\times 600 = 582,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   0 + 48,\\!550 + 582,\\!600 = 631,\\!150\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{631,\\!150}\n\\]",
