      "text": "349,900.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **605** and **580**, we'll follow a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. **Multiply 605 by 0 (the ones place digit of 580):**\n   \n   \\[\n   605 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 605 by 80 (the tens place digit of 580):**\n   \n   \\[\n   605 \\times 80 = 48,400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 605 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 580):**\n   \n   \\[\n   605 \\times 500 = 302,500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   0 + 48,400 + 302,500 = 350,900\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{350,\\!900}\n\\]",
