      "text": "17,880.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe product of **140** and **127** is **17,880**.\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **140** and **127**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 140 by 7 (the ones place digit of 127):**\n   \n   \\[\n   140 \\times 7 = 980\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 140 by 20 (the tens place digit of 127):**\n   \n   \\[\n   140 \\times 20 = 2,800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 140 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 127):**\n   \n   \\[\n   140 \\times 100 = 14,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   980 + 2,800 + 14,000 = 17,780\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{17,\\!780}\n\\]",
