      "text": "123,456.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **217** and **568**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 217 by 8 (the ones place digit of 568):**\n   \n   \\[\n   217 \\times 8 = 1736\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 217 by 60 (the tens place digit of 568):**\n   \n   \\[\n   217 \\times 60 = 13020\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 217 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 568):**\n   \n   \\[\n   217 \\times 500 = 108500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1736 + 13020 + 108500 = 123456\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{123456}\n\\]",
