      "text": "56,440.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **340** and **166**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 340 by 6 (the ones place digit of 166):**\n   \n   \\[\n   340 \\times 6 = 2040\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 340 by 60 (the tens place digit of 166):**\n   \n   \\[\n   340 \\times 60 = 20,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 340 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 166):**\n   \n   \\[\n   340 \\times 100 = 34,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2,\\!040 + 20,\\!400 + 34,\\!000 = 56,\\!440\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{56,\\!440}\n\\]",
