      "text": "58,848.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **414** and **142**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 414 by 2 (the ones place digit of 142):**\n   \n   \\[\n   414 \\times 2 = 828\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 414 by 40 (the tens place digit of 142):**\n   \n   \\[\n   414 \\times 40 = 16,\\!560\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 414 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 142):**\n   \n   \\[\n   414 \\times 100 = 41,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   828 + 16,\\!560 + 41,\\!400 = 58,\\!848\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{58,\\!848}\n\\]",
