      "index": 0,
      "text": "256,  240.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check the calculations.\n\n1. 560 \u00d7 8 = 4480\n2. 560 \u00d7 50 = 28,000\n3. 560 \u00d7 400 = 224,000\n\nNow, sum all the results:\n\n4480 + 28,000 = 32,480\n\n32,480 + 224,000 = 256,480\n\nSo, the final product is 256,480.\n\n**Answer:**\nThe product of 560 and 458 is \\boxed{256480}.",
