      "text": "15222.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe product of 122 and 126 is **15,222**.\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of 122 and 126, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 122 by 6 (the ones place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 6 = 732\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 122 by 20 (the tens place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 20 = 2,440\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 122 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 100 = 12,200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   732 + 2,440 + 12,200 = 15,222\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15,\\!222}\n\\]",
