      "text": "481,920.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **960** and **502**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 960 by 2 (the ones place digit of 502):**\n   \n   \\[\n   960 \\times 2 = 1,\\!920\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 960 by 0 (the tens place digit of 502):**\n   \n   \\[\n   960 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 960 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 502):**\n   \n   \\[\n   960 \\times 500 = 480,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1,\\!920 + 0 + 480,\\!000 = 481,\\!920\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{481,\\!920}\n\\]",
