      "index": 0,
      "text": "129,120.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **480** and **269**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 480 by each digit of 269\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   480 \\times 9 = 4320\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   480 \\times 60 = 28,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   480 \\times 200 = 96,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n4320 + 28,\\!800 + 96,\\!000 = 129,\\!120\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{129,\\!120}\n\\]",
