      "index": 0,
      "text": "642,562.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **692** and **926**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 692 by 6 (the ones place digit of 926):**\n   \n   \\[\n   692 \\times 6 = 4152\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 692 by 20 (the tens place digit of 926):**\n   \n   \\[\n   692 \\times 20 = 13840\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 692 by 900 (the hundreds place digit of 926):**\n   \n   \\[\n   692 \\times 900 = 622800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   4152 + 13840 + 622800 = 642562\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{642562}\n\\]",
