      "text": "174,  1280 + 44,800 + 128,000 = 174,  1280 + 44,800 = 46,080; 46,080 + 128,000 = 174,080.\n\nThe final computed product is 174,080.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **640** and **272**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 640 by each digit of 272\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   640 \\times 2 = 1,\\!280\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (7), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   640 \\times 70 = 44,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (2), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   640 \\times 200 = 128,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1,\\!280 + 44,\\!800 + 128,\\!000 = 174,\\!080\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{174,\\!080}\n\\]",
