      "text": "645,985.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **969** and **665**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 969 by 5 (the ones place digit of 665)\n\\[\n969 \\times 5 = 4,\\!845\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 969 by 60 (the tens place digit of 665)\n\\[\n969 \\times 60 = 58,\\!140\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 969 by 600 (the hundreds place digit of 665)\n\\[\n969 \\times 600 = 581,\\!400\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum all the results\n\\[\n4,\\!845 + 58,\\!140 + 581,\\!400 = 645,\\!985\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{645,\\!985}\n\\]",
