      "index": 0,
      "text": "767,561.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nTo find the product of **957** and **803**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 957 by 3 (the ones place digit of 803):**\n   \n   \\[\n   957 \\times 3 = 2,\\!871\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 957 by 0 (the tens place digit of 803):**\n   \n   \\[\n   957 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 957 by 800 (the hundreds place digit of 803):**\n   \n   \\[\n   957 \\times 800 = 765,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2,\\!871 + 0 + 765,\\!600 = 767,\\!561\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{767,\\!561}\n\\]",
