      "index": 0,
      "text": "82,320.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **580** and **144**, we'll follow a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. **Multiply 580 by the ones place digit of 144 (which is 4):**\n   \n   \\[\n   580 \\times 4 = 2320\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 580 by the tens place digit of 144 (which is 4, representing 40):**\n   \n   \\[\n   580 \\times 40 = 23200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 580 by the hundreds place digit of 144 (which is 1, representing 100):**\n   \n   \\[\n   580 \\times 100 = 58000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2320 + 23200 + 58000 = 82320\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{82,\\!320}\n\\]",
