      "text": "115,444.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **268** and **433**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 268 by the ones place digit of 433\n\\[\n268 \\times 3 = 804\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 268 by the tens place digit of 433 (remember to add a zero)\n\\[\n268 \\times 30 = 8040\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 268 by the hundreds place digit of 433 (remember to add two zeros)\n\\[\n268 \\times 400 = 107,\\!200\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum all the results\n\\[\n804 + 8,\\!040 + 107,\\!200 = 115,\\!444\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{115,\\!444}\n\\]",
